# Build context for apps/demo/Dockerfile is the repo root, and that Dockerfile
# copies whole directories (`COPY packages packages`, `COPY apps/demo apps/demo`).
# Without these excludes the image would vary with whatever happens to be sitting
# in a developer's working tree, so a locally built image and the one CI builds
# would not be the same artifact.
#
# Patterns are matched from the context root, so nested matches need `**/` --
# a bare `node_modules` would exclude only the top-level one and still copy in
# apps/demo/node_modules and packages/*/node_modules.

# Installed in-image by `bun install`; copying host trees in would both bloat the
# image and shadow that install with symlinks pointing at a store that isn't there.
**/node_modules

# The container runs TypeScript straight from packages/*/src via the CMD's
# `--conditions @maelstrom-co/source`, so no build output belongs in it.
**/dist
**/.output
**/.nx
**/.wrangler
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Nothing in the image reads these: the container takes HOSTED=1 from ENV and
# the visitor's key over the playground.hello handshake. VITE_* vars are
# build-time for the client bundle, which CI builds outside this image.
**/.env
**/.env.*

.git
.jj
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
